+      <article id="journal-article" class="journal-content">
+        <p>
+          Every exceptional cup of coffee begins long before the first crack in our cast-iron drum roasters—it starts on high-altitude volcanic slopes where microclimates, shade canopies, and generational farming wisdom converge. At The Daily Grind, our bean sourcing process is built exclusively on direct-trade partnerships with smallholder cooperatives across Ethiopia's Yirgacheffe region, Colombia's Huila highlands, and Guatemala's Antigua valley. Rather than purchasing anonymous commodity lots through distant brokers, we travel to origin twice each harvest cycle to walk the terraces alongside our partner producers, inspect soil health, and cup freshly milled parchment lots right at the washing station.
+        </p>
+        <p>
+          Sustainability and biodiversity guide every purchasing commitment we make. We exclusively source shade-grown Arabica varietals—including Heirloom, Bourbon, Caturra, and Geisha—cultivated beneath native inga and wild fig trees. This natural canopy slows cherry maturation, allowing complex sugars and vibrant organic acids to develop inside the seed while providing vital habitat for migratory songbirds and preventing hillside erosion. During peak harvest, pickers selectively harvest only deep-crimson cherries by hand, passing over under-ripe fruit for subsequent picking rounds to ensure uniform sweetness in every lot.
+        </p>
+        <p>
+          Once harvested, processing precision determines the clarity of the final cup. Depending on local water resources and regional traditions, our partner mills employ either washed fermentation in spring-water channels with solar-raised African drying beds, or honey and natural sun-dried methods that preserve lush stone-fruit and floral aromatics. Samples are air-freighted to our roastery lab where we grade green beans for moisture content, water activity, and zero primary defects—requiring a minimum Specialty Coffee Association (SCA) cupping score of 86 points before signing a contract.
+        </p>
+        <p>
+          Finally, financial transparency anchors the entire supply chain. We pay farmers a guaranteed floor price at least 45% above Fair Trade minimums, plus quality-tier bonuses tied directly to cupping scores, and we pre-finance up to 60% of the harvest value before export so cooperatives can invest in wet-mill upgrades, organic composting programs, and community healthcare. Once sealed in GrainPro hermetic liners and shipped to our local roastery, each micro-lot is small-batch roasted to highlight the terroir and craftsmanship of the people who grew it.
+        </p>
+      </article>
+
